&lt;p&gt;Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu has shared a warning by author Yuval Bloomberg about Iran&amp;rsquo;s efforts to acquire nuclear weapons, describing the prospect as an existential threat to Israel. Bloomberg argued that the country faced a &amp;ldquo;real and concrete&amp;rdquo; danger and said the situation would change fundamentally if Tehran obtained a nuclear weapon. He urged Israel to prioritise what he called completing the mission in Iran, saying domestic disputes were distracting attention from the country&amp;rsquo;s most pressing security concern ahead of its elections.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&amp;lsquo;Existential Threat&amp;rsquo;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Netanyahu shared Bloomberg&amp;rsquo;s comments in a post on X on Sunday. Bloomberg said Israel had two years remaining under US President Donald Trump to complete the task in Iran, adding that the future after Trump&amp;rsquo;s term was uncertain.&lt;/p&gt;
